<title>BELGIUM: BELGIUM/LUX 1996 CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS REV DOWN.</title>
<headline>BELGIUM/LUX 1996 CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS REV DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Belgium</p>
<p>(NBB) said on Friday it had revised down its estimate of the</p>
<p>1996 current account surplus of the Belgium Luxembourg Economic</p>
<p>Union (BLEU) to 387 from 391 billion Belgian francs.</p>
<p>The 1995 surplus had been revised up to 351 from 346 billion</p>
<p>francs, the central bank said in its weekly economic indicators</p>
<p>publication.</p>
<p>The current account is a measure of a country's financial</p>
<p>position with the rest of the world, measuring trade in goods</p>
<p>and services. Belgium and Luxembourg have been joined in a</p>
<p>currency union since the 1920s.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax</p>
<p>+32 2 230 7710</p>
